    "description": "Original MCQs for a workplace IT-security / cyber-hygiene awareness module aimed at general employees (no IT-specialist or audit-level detail). Content is independently phrased and grounded in publicly available guidance: BSI IT-Grundschutz-Kompendium Bausteine (e.g. ORP.3, ORP.4, CON.3, DER.2.1, OPS.1.2.4, SYS.3.2.1) and BSI consumer/employee phishing guidance, ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Annex A control themes described conceptually (not a certification-exam simulation), and the EU NIS2 Directive's general employee-relevant obligations (Art. 21(2)(g) cyber hygiene practices and training; Art. 23 incident reporting timelines). This is a fully independent exam module from Fuehrerschein (Klasse B), Motorrad and Angelschein - separate content pool, separate exam simulation. Locales: de (canonical), en (reviewed translation) for this first round. Expanded 2026-08-13 with 3 new topic categories (social_engineering, ransomware, ki_bedrohungen) closing a documented content gap versus the closest EU direct competitor's (SoSafe) core catalog - see claude/compliance-competitor-pricing-and-course-gaps.md section 3. Grounded in the same BSI IT-Grundschutz-Kompendium Bausteine style as the original 5 categories (ORP.3/ORP.4/OPS.1.1.3/DER.2.1/CON.3), plus general BSI Lagebericht framing for the newer KI/deepfake-threat questions where no single settled statutory citation exists yet. legal_review_status unchanged - still NOT legally reviewed.",
